From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] venus: keep VK_KHR_incremental_present in the guest

What: treat VK_KHR_incremental_present like VK_KHR_swapchain when creating
the renderer-side device: block it (and the other guest-WSI extensions)
from the host's extension list.
Why: venus lists VK_KHR_incremental_present itself (common WSI), but only
strips the WSI extensions when the app also enables VK_KHR_swapchain.
Chrome's ANGLE on Vulkan enables incremental_present without a swapchain,
venus forwards it, and a host driver without it (KosmicKrisp, MoltenVK)
fails vkCreateDevice with VK_ERROR_EXTENSION_NOT_PRESENT: no ANGLE on
Vulkan in Chrome at all.
Upstream: upstreamable to Mesa (src/virtio/vulkan), not sent.
Applies to: Mesa main e5f0687867f5 (guest build, /opt/mesa-kk).
Test: Chrome 154 --use-angle=vulkan in the VM: chrome://gpu shows
"ANGLE (Apple, Vulkan 1.4.334 (Virtio-GPU Venus (Apple M4)))", WebGL 2.

--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_device.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_device.c
@@ -258,7 +258,8 @@
 
    /* fix for WSI (treat AHB as WSI extension for simplicity) */
    const bool has_wsi =
-      app_exts->KHR_swapchain || app_exts->ANDROID_native_buffer ||
+      app_exts->KHR_swapchain || app_exts->KHR_incremental_present ||
+      app_exts->ANDROID_native_buffer ||
       app_exts->ANDROID_external_memory_android_hardware_buffer;
    if (has_wsi) {
       if (renderer_exts->EXT_image_drm_format_modifier &&
@@ -279,7 +280,7 @@
             VK_EXT_QUEUE_FAMILY_FOREIGN_EXTENSION_NAME;
       }
 
-      if (app_exts->KHR_swapchain) {
+      if (app_exts->KHR_swapchain || app_exts->KHR_incremental_present) {
          /* see vn_physical_device_get_native_extensions */
          block_exts[block_count++] = VK_KHR_PRESENT_ID_EXTENSION_NAME;
          block_exts[block_count++] = VK_KHR_PRESENT_ID_2_EXTENSION_NAME;
